{
	"_about": "rowan: a 79s dark canvas-editor launch film, derived frame-by-frame from a 79.1s launch film for an AI design canvas (1812x1080 @30fps). Authored in reference px inside a 1812x1080 box on the 1280x720 stage (stage px = ref px / 1.5, centred), rendered at device scale 1.5: render.mjs --fps 30 --scale 1.5. Placeholder product: Rowan (rowan.example), an AI design canvas whose agent designs a wind-farm control room, a bakery site and a design system. ONE app window lies on a black backdrop of white contour ribbons; the camera is two slow linear centred pushes that run under every cut; the interior changes by hard cuts and four dips to black; three short mono captions name the late features; a typed mono end card closes.",
	"_sections": "S1 0-14.6 CLI on the canvas, prompt close-up, chat card, the artboard building itself | S2 14.6-46.6 six finished takes cutting under one push, dip, 2x2 and 3x3 boards, phone row, zoom onto three phones | S3 46.6-73.0 site on the canvas, dip, design-to-code terminal (x1.37 punch), dip, coded site in a browser, dip, design-system page with slots, variables, light flip, mesh gradient | S4 73.0-79.1 typed end card: claim, then url",
	"_slots": "Every rowan-shot scene takes `src` (an .mp4 screen recording of YOUR app window, plus `clip`) and then shows it inside the window instead of the drawn stand-in; keep the camera keys. Pictures inside the drawn views are image slots under `images`: `hero` (variant/build), `cell-N` (boards), `site-1`..`site-6` (site, code, browser). Without them, drawn stand-ins.",
